nomials for all rounds\n\n#### 3.1 SEGMENT TREE BUILDING (Lines 517-576)\n\nThis phase builds the binary tree bottom-up in the GPU:\n\n1. **Bit-reversal + Layer 0+1 fusion** (lines 525-557):\n   - If `total_leaves > 1024`: Fuses three operations into one CUDA kernel via `bit_rev_frac_ext_build_k2()` (line 529)\n   - Otherwise: Separate `bit_rev_frac_ext()` + `frac_build_tree_layer()` (lines 535-555)\n\n2. **Two-layer fusion loop** (lines 560-568):\n   - For each pair of consecutive layers, calls `frac_build_tree_two_layers()` (line 564)\n   - CUDA kernel fuses layers `i` and `i+1` into one pass\n\n3. **Remaining single layer** (lines 570-575):\n   - If odd number of layers remains, calls `frac_build_tree_layer()` (line 572)\n\n4. **Root copy and final revert** (lines 578-583):\n   - `copy_from_device()` to get root value (line 579) - **SYNCHRONIZATION POINT**\n   - `frac_build_tree_layer(..., revert=true)` (line 581) for tree revert\n\n**Sequential Pattern Identified:**\n- Tree building is **purely sequential** in terms of layers\n- Each layer depends on the previous one\n- No parallelization across layers possible in current design\n- Multiple GPU kernels launched in sequence\n\n#### 3.2 FIRST LAYER CLAIMS AND SETUP (Lines 596-654)\n\n1. **Copy first left/right values** (lines 599-606) - **SYNCHRONIZATION POINTS**\n   - `copy_from_device()` twice (lines 599-600)\n   - Blocks CPU until GPU values copied to host\n\n2. **Observer pattern** (lines 607-614):\n   - Observe four claim values in transcript\n\n3. **Buffer allocation and setup** (lines 617-654):\n   - Allocates work buffers for ping-pong computations\n   - Allocates eq buffer layers from CPU (`SqrtEqLayers::from_xi()`, line 663)\n\n#### 3.3 GKR ROUNDS MAIN LOOP (Lines 655-1079)\n\n**Loop structure:** `for round in 1..total_rounds` (line 655)\n- Each iteration processes one GKR sumcheck round\n\n**PER-ROUND OPERATIONS:**\n\n1. **Eq buffer initialization** (line 663):\n   - `SqrtEqLayers::from_xi()` - CPU-side