on. But the real question is GPU utilization—with 4 threads, I'm only activating 4-16 SMs out of 128, which is severely underutilized. Going to 8 or 16 threads would activate more SMs and potentially improve overall throughput despite the CPU-side contention.\n\nThe lock overhead from those ~12,000+ acquisitions is probably negligible—maybe 19ms total across all threads. The actual bottleneck is likely memory bandwidth and pool contention. But here's the key insight: at APC 0, the threshold prevents multi-threading entirely since there are fewer than 100 AIRs, so increasing thread count wouldn't even affect that case. Only at APC 100+ would the multi-threading kick in.\n\nFor APC 100, we're looking at roughly 15 AIRs per thread with 8 threads, which might not give much overlap benefit. But at APC 300 with ~39 AIRs per thread, there's still decent opportunity for parallelism. Let me examine this from another angle to see where the real gains would come from.\n\nNow I'm checking whether the Round 0, MLE, and GKR phases are pipelined or if there's idle time between them.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":883,"cache_read_input_tokens":100782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":883},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6440d5e-5fb7-4583-a464-0e3f9791a04a","uuid":"c7f6d72a-025d-4773-88d3-e5a896e23028"}
