{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BcwWssiM9i8PR91i7gAwbM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1500-batch-stacking-scatter-kernel\n2\t\n3\tThe `stack_traces_into_expanded()` function in `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` iterates over every trace column (~106K at APC 300) issuing individual CUDA API calls (cudaMemcpyAsync or batch_expand_pad_wide kernel launch) per column. At ~1us CPU overhead per call, this loop costs ~100ms—about 25% of the 404ms Trace Commit phase and 6% of STARK excl trace. Replacing the per-column loop with a single batched scatter kernel that processes all column copies in one GPU launch eliminates this CPU-side overhead, reducing Trace Commit by ~100ms at APC 300 with negligible impact at APC 0 (only ~4K columns).\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6440d5e-5fb7-4583-a464-0e3f9791a04a","uuid":"d4284a8b-374c-4473-a98f-789c9775e7f4","timestamp":"2026-04-13T03:16:34.497Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1500-batch-stacking-scatter-kernel\n\nThe `stack_traces_into_expanded()` function in `crates/cuda-backend/src/stacked_pcs.rs` iterates over every trace column (~106K at APC 300) issuing individual CUDA API calls (cudaMemcpyAsync or batch_expand_pad_wide kernel launch) per column. At ~1us CPU overhead per call, this loop costs ~100ms—about 25% of the 404ms Trace Commit phase and 6% of STARK excl trace. Replacing the per-column loop with a single batched scatter kernel that processes all column copies in one GPU launch eliminates this CPU-side overhead, reducing Trace Commit by ~100ms at APC 300 with negligible impact at APC 0 (only ~4K columns).\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RwYZVw9byAMEsGHsRSwKEL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NFvPJ3kNXsRkXDYgWfSRN4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1830-increase-multistream-thread-count\n\nIncrease the multi-stream thread count from 4 to 8 for both Round 0 (`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`) and GKR input evaluation (`log_gkr_input_evals`). At APC 300, each segment has ~310 AIRs launching kernels that occupy only 1-4 of the RTX 4090's 128 SMs. With 4 threads, effective parallelism is only 1.7-2.1x (measured via nsys kernel time vs wall time). Doubling to 8 threads increases concurrent kernel occupancy and reduces per-chunk imbalance, targeting a ~100-150ms reduction in STARK excl trace at APC 300.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":414,"cache_read_input_tokens":166401,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":414},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6440d5e-5fb7-4583-a464-0e3f9791a04a","uuid":"8ab86180-25af-4b9b-89d4-d19a6f0476db"}
