{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TRYfapqKv2cFmj7aDkNBte","type":"tool_result","content":"73\t// l_skip)` but the `leading_zeros` calculation below is easier to check in the recursion\n74\t// circuit. The formula below is equivalent to `log2_ceil(total_interactions + 1) - l_skip`.\n75\tpub fn calculate_n_logup(l_skip: usize, total_interactions: u64) -> usize {\n76\t    if total_interactions != 0 {\n77\t        let n_logup = (u64::BITS - total_interactions.leading_zeros()) as usize - l_skip;\n78\t        debug_assert_eq!(\n79\t            n_logup + l_skip,\n80\t            log2_ceil_u64(total_interactions + 1) as usize\n81\t        );\n82\t        n_logup"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6ojr9DPp1tgy7dbuQbzdu","session_id":"e6440d5e-5fb7-4583-a464-0e3f9791a04a","uuid":"8097a6c5-cd84-49b3-a9e9-d64f7b9f2d67","timestamp":"2026-04-13T03:20:05.345Z"}
